Z||000000||dman||06-22-2001||11:33 PM||||Hello everyone. I have an automatic fiero that I need to tow approximately 10 to 20 miles. This car has front end damage so I'll need to tow it with the front end up. (and no, a flatbed is probably not an option)<P>This of course is not an ideal thing to do since this car has an auto transmission. Also most of the weight of a fiero is in the rear.<P>Assuming I don't go over 35mph, is there any real chance of hurting the transmission?<P>Thanks in advance.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||starfighter007@msn.com||06-23-2001||12:27 AM||||I am no expert in the field of towing but I think if you are only going 10 to 20 miles @35 Mph I dont think you will do any damage? I think whe you tow any car with the drive wheels any damage that does happen ,happens when you tow long distances and at high speeds I believe what happens is the transmision becomes very hot and over heated as no fluid is beig pumped thru the radiator.but I think you can tow any car on the drive wheels up to 50 miles.hope fully someone here with more knowledge than I will vrify what I am saying or set you straight goodluck||||reg||4
Z||000002||isthiswhereiputausername?||06-23-2001||12:34 AM||||I towed my fiero 30 miles before with no damage.<BR>(stopped halfway for 10 minutes to let both cars cool off-hot day)<P>I wouldnt worry about your short distance.. Just keep the speed down  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fierowrecker||06-23-2001||01:33 AM||||Hey Dman!<BR>Keep the speed at 25 to 30 MPH and you should be fine...<BR>So wha happen?<BR>Accident?<BR>Buying a parts car??<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||06-23-2001||12:19 PM||||A short distance like that should not be a problem. Especially if you keep the speed down.<P>Usually when we are talking about towing here it's for long trips. On long trips, it does matter how you do it.||||reg||1
